---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
import CTABlock from '../components/CTABlock.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Invite someone | Search OC"
	description="Three texts you can actually send, and what to say when they ask something you can't answer."
	canonical="/invite"
	ogImage="/og/invite.png"
	ogDescription="Three texts you can actually send, and what to say when they ask something you can't answer."
/>

<!-- Hero -->
<section class="hero-gradient">
	<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-12 md:pt-20">
		<div class="max-w-3xl">
			<Eyebrow text="For the person doing the inviting" variant="amber" />
			<h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-[1.1]">
				You have someone in mind. Here is how to ask.
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-5 lead">
				You already know who. You just do not know how to bring it up without it getting weird. That is what this page is for.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- The ask is smaller -->
<section class="section">
	<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
		<div class="max-w-3xl">
			<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">The ask is smaller than you think</h2>
			<p class="mt-6 text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
				You are not inviting anyone to church. You are inviting them to one table, for one hour, to talk about one honest question. Eight to twelve people, food, no sermon, no follow-up unless they ask for it.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
				They can come once and never come back, and nothing about your friendship changes. That is the whole deal. It is small on purpose.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4">
				<a href="/open-forums" class="font-sans font-semibold text-[var(--search-blue)] hover:underline">See exactly what a night looks like &rarr;</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- Three texts -->
<section class="section-warm section">
	<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
		<div class="max-w-3xl">
			<Eyebrow text="Copy and send" />
			<h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Three texts you can actually send</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-[var(--muted)]">
				Steal these. Change the words so they sound like you, then send it today while you still mean it.
			</p>

			<div class="mt-8 space-y-6">
				<div class="card">
					<Eyebrow text="A close friend" />
					<div class="mt-3 border border-[var(--border)] rounded-xl p-5 bg-[var(--surface)]">
						<p>Random one for you. I go to this thing where eight or so people sit around a table over dinner and argue about God for an hour. Nobody preaches, nobody is selling anything. Honestly I just think you'd have things to say. Want to come with me?</p>
					</div>
					<button class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold font-sans text-[var(--search-blue)] hover:underline copy-btn" data-target="text-1">Copy</button>
				</div>

				<div class="card">
					<Eyebrow text="Someone you work with" />
					<div class="mt-3 border border-[var(--border)] rounded-xl p-5 bg-[var(--surface)]">
						<p>This is a little out of left field. There's a group I'm part of that gets a handful of people around a table over dinner and takes on one big question, like whether suffering makes God impossible. It's an hour, it's not a church thing, and you can disagree with everyone in the room. I thought of you. Any interest?</p>
					</div>
					<button class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold font-sans text-[var(--search-blue)] hover:underline copy-btn" data-target="text-2">Copy</button>
				</div>

				<div class="card">
					<Eyebrow text="Someone church has burned" />
					<div class="mt-3 border border-[var(--border)] rounded-xl p-5 bg-[var(--surface)]">
						<p>I want to run something by you, and it is completely fine to say no. There's a table I go to where people ask the questions about God that churches usually dodge. No worship, no sermon, no one is going to corner you at the end. The people who have been burned are usually the ones who make the night worth it. If you ever want to come, I'll sit next to you.</p>
					</div>
					<button class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold font-sans text-[var(--search-blue)] hover:underline copy-btn" data-target="text-3">Copy</button>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- Can't answer -->
<section class="section">
	<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
		<div class="max-w-3xl">
			<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">"What if they ask me something I can't answer?"</h2>
			<p class="mt-6 callout text-base not-italic">
				You say: "I don't know. Come ask it out loud."
			</p>
			<p class="mt-6 text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
				That is it. That is the entire thing you have to be able to do.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
				You are not the expert and you were never supposed to be. You are the door. The table is where the question gets handled, and a question you can't answer is the best possible reason for them to show up.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
				The fastest way to lose someone is to bluff. "I don't know" is the most credible sentence you own. Use it.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- Two things -->
<section class="section-warm section">
	<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
		<div class="max-w-3xl">
			<Eyebrow text="Hold onto these" />
			<h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Two things to hold onto</h2>
			<div class="mt-8 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
				<div class="card">
					<h3 class="font-sans font-bold text-lg">God is responsible for the results.</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
						Your job is the invitation. Whether they come, what they think, what happens in them after, none of that is yours to carry. Show up, prepare, use what you've been given. Let go of the rest.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3 class="font-sans font-bold text-lg">A spiritual journey is a process.</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
						Nobody arrives in one conversation. One honest hour at a table is a real step, even if it is the only one you ever see. You are probably not the first person in this story and you will not be the last.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- If they say no -->
<section class="section-tight">
	<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
		<div class="max-w-3xl callout">
			<h3 class="font-sans font-semibold text-[var(--ink)] not-italic">If they say no</h3>
			<p class="mt-2 not-italic text-[var(--muted)]">
				Then you know where they are, which is more than you knew yesterday. You asked once, gently, and you didn't make it strange. Ask again next year. That is a fine outcome.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- CTA Form -->
<section id="cta" class="section">
	<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
		<div class="max-w-xl">
			<Eyebrow text="Get the date" variant="amber" />
			<h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">You will want to know the date</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
				Hard to invite anyone to a night that doesn't have a date yet. Leave your email and you'll know the moment the next table is set, early enough to ask before it fills.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-3 text-[var(--muted)]">
				If you already know who you're bringing, put their first name in. I'll watch for them and sit them somewhere good.
			</p>

			<form id="invite-form" class="mt-6 space-y-4" method="POST" action="/api/invite">
				<div>
					<label for="email" class="block text-sm font-medium font-sans text-[var(--dark-teal)] mb-1">Your email</label>
					<input type="email" id="email" name="email" required class="input" autocomplete="email" />
				</div>
				<div>
					<label for="guestName" class="block text-sm font-medium font-sans text-[var(--dark-teal)] mb-1">Who you're bringing (optional, first name is plenty)</label>
					<input type="text" id="guestName" name="guestName" class="input" autocomplete="off" />
				</div>
				<button type="submit" id="submit-btn" class="btn-amber w-full min-h-11 inline-flex items-center justify-center">
					Keep me in the loop
				</button>
				<p class="text-xs text-[var(--cool-gray)] font-sans">Two things show up in your inbox: the date of the next table, and Having Killer Conversations, a short note every other week for Christians who want to talk about their faith without being weird about it. Nothing else, and you can leave any time.</p>
			</form>

			<div id="form-success" class="hidden mt-6 card text-[var(--muted)]">
				<p class="font-sans font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">You are in. I will email you the second the next table has a date.</p>
			</div>

			<div id="form-error" class="hidden mt-4 text-sm text-red-600 font-sans">
				That did not go through, which is on us, not you. Try again in a minute.
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<script is:inline>
	document.querySelectorAll('.copy-btn').forEach((btn) => {
		btn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
			const targetId = btn.getAttribute('data-target');
			const textMap = {
				'text-1': 'Random one for you. I go to this thing where eight or so people sit around a table over dinner and argue about God for an hour. Nobody preaches, nobody is selling anything. Honestly I just think you\'d have things to say. Want to come with me?',
				'text-2': "This is a little out of left field. There's a group I'm part of that gets a handful of people around a table over dinner and takes on one big question, like whether suffering makes God impossible. It's an hour, it's not a church thing, and you can disagree with everyone in the room. I thought of you. Any interest?",
				'text-3': 'I want to run something by you, and it is completely fine to say no. There\'s a table I go to where people ask the questions about God that churches usually dodge. No worship, no sermon, no one is going to corner you at the end. The people who have been burned are usually the ones who make the night worth it. If you ever want to come, I\'ll sit next to you.'
			};
			const text = textMap[targetId];
			if (!text) return;
			try {
				await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
				btn.textContent = 'Copied';
				btn.disabled = true;
				setTimeout(() => { btn.textContent = 'Copy'; btn.disabled = false; }, 2000);
			} catch {}
		});
	});

	const form = document.getElementById('invite-form');
	const success = document.getElementById('form-success');
	const errorBox = document.getElementById('form-error');
	const submitBtn = document.getElementById('submit-btn');

	if (form && success && errorBox && submitBtn) {
		form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
			e.preventDefault();
			success.classList.add('hidden');
			errorBox.classList.add('hidden');

			const formData = new FormData(form);
			const email = (formData.get('email') || '').toString().trim();

			if (!email || !email.includes('@')) {
				errorBox.textContent = 'Please enter a valid email.';
				errorBox.classList.remove('hidden');
				return;
			}

			submitBtn.disabled = true;
			submitBtn.textContent = 'Sending...';

			try {
				const res = await fetch('/api/invite', {
					method: 'POST',
					headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
					body: JSON.stringify({
						email: email,
						guestName: (formData.get('guestName') || '').toString().trim()
					})
				});
				if (res.ok) {
					form.classList.add('hidden');
					success.classList.remove('hidden');
				} else {
					throw new Error('Submission failed');
				}
			} catch {
				errorBox.textContent = 'That did not go through, which is on us, not you. Try again in a minute.';
				errorBox.classList.remove('hidden');
			} finally {
				submitBtn.disabled = false;
				submitBtn.textContent = 'Keep me in the loop';
			}
		});
	}
</script>
